        // A player's SCORE pays out as the room's currency (Silver in Crescendo, Gold on the Isle)
        // when the game posts it to the leaderboard: the accepted write pays (new score - the score
        // already stored for that player on that board). The checkpoint award the game itself
        // sends is a flat 1000 - the client never sends the score with it, so the score can only
        // be paid where the server actually sees it, which is the leaderboard post at the end of
        // the run. Gated by the same LeaderboardGuard as the leaderboard itself.
        /// <summary>
